{"id":21648,"date":"2026-07-17T11:53:17","date_gmt":"2026-07-17T11:53:17","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/?p=21648"},"modified":"2026-08-03T09:56:40","modified_gmt":"2026-08-03T09:56:40","slug":"most-visited-websites","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/most-visited-websites\/","title":{"rendered":"Top 100 Most Visited Websites in the World (2026 Traffic Data)"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>The internet has more than 1.1 billion live websites today, yet only a tiny fraction of them&nbsp;pull&nbsp;in the bulk of global traffic. A handful of platforms, search engines, social networks, AI tools, and shopping sites, absorb billions of visits every single month while the rest of the web fights for the leftovers.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you have ever wondered which sites actually rule the internet in 2026, you are in the right place.&nbsp;This guide breaks down the&nbsp;most visited websites in the world, ranked using traffic data from Similarweb (June 2026), and explains why each one holds its position.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Whether you want to know the&nbsp;world&#8217;s most visited website, compare platforms by category, or study the&nbsp;top 100 most visited websites in the world, this article covers it all in one place.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Which Is the Most Visited Website in the World? (Quick Answer)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Google.com&nbsp;is the&nbsp;most visited website in the world&nbsp;in 2026, drawing tens of billions of monthly visits through Search, Maps, Gmail, and its AI-powered search features. YouTube holds second place as the largest video platform, followed closely by Facebook and Instagram. Together, these four sites&nbsp;alone account&nbsp;for a massive share of all web traffic worldwide.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the World<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Here is a dedicated look at the&nbsp;top 10 most visited websites in the world&nbsp;right now, based on the latest Similarweb rankings.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Rank<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>Website<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>Monthly Traffic (Visits)<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><td><strong>Category<\/strong>&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1&nbsp;<\/td><td>Google.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>94.8 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Search Engine&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>2&nbsp;<\/td><td>YouTube.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>47.5 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Video Streaming&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3&nbsp;<\/td><td>Facebook.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>11.8 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Social Media&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4&nbsp;<\/td><td>Instagram.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>7.4&nbsp;billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Social Media&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>5&nbsp;<\/td><td>ChatGPT.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>5.6 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>AI Chatbot&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>6&nbsp;<\/td><td>X.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>4.8&nbsp;billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Social Media&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>7&nbsp;<\/td><td>Reddit.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>4.4&nbsp;billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Social Media \/ Community&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>8&nbsp;<\/td><td>WhatsApp.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>3.7 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Messaging&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>9&nbsp;<\/td><td>Bing.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>3.3&nbsp;billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Search Engine&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10&nbsp;<\/td><td>TikTok.com&nbsp;<\/td><td>3.6 billion&nbsp;<\/td><td>Social Media&nbsp;<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>A few things stand out&nbsp;in&nbsp;this list. Google&nbsp;remains&nbsp;untouchable at the top, and it has held that spot for well over a decade. YouTube, which Google also owns, generates more traffic than the next several sites on this list combined, proving that video content is still the biggest driver of attention online.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The most interesting shift is ChatGPT landing at number five. It is the first time in internet history that an AI chatbot has broken into the global t