-faq-answer\">Facebook is the world&#8217;s most visited social media website by web traffic. However, platforms like Instagram, TikTok, and WhatsApp also enjoy massive engagement, especially through mobile apps.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784282996244\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">4. Which educational website receives the most visitors?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Wikipedia is the world&#8217;s most visited educational and reference website. Millions of people use it daily to access free, reliable information on history, science, technology, culture, and more.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283010968\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">5. Which news websites receive the highest traffic?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Popular news websites include Yahoo News, CNN, BBC, The New York Times, and MSN. Their rankings vary throughout the year depending on breaking news, global events, and audience demand.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283025284\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">6. Are website rankings the same in every country?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No. Website rankings differ by country because internet users have different languages, interests, and browsing habits. Local platforms often outperform global websites in several regional markets.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283037598\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">7. What is the most visited website in India?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Google is the most visited website in India, followed by YouTube. Indians use Google extensively for search, while YouTube dominates video streaming, education, entertainment, and learning content.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283053023\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">8. Which is the most visited website in the world?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Google.com is the world&#8217;s most visited website, consistently holding the top position due to its dominance in online search, navigation, maps, productivity tools, and the wider Google ecosystem.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283065738\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">9. What is the world&#8217;s most visited website after Google?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">YouTube.com ranks second among the world&#8217;s most visited websites. It is followed by Facebook and Instagram, which continue to attract billions of users through video, social networking, and content sharing.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283079519\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">10. Which is the most popular AI website right now?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">ChatGPT.com is currently the most popular AI website, attracting millions of users for writing, coding, research, and productivity. Gemini, Claude, and DeepSeek are also experiencing rapid growth worldwide.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283096177\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">11. Do these rankings include app traffic?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No. Website traffic rankings from platforms like Similarweb and\u00a0Semrush\u00a0measure web visits only. They exclude app usage, meaning platforms like WhatsApp, Instagram, and TikTok have much higher overall audiences.<\/p> <\/div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1784283111431\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\">12. What is the fastest-growing website category in 2026?<\/strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">AI platforms are the fastest-growing website category in 2026. Services such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and DeepSeek continue expanding rapidly as individuals and businesses increasingly adopt AI-powered tools.<\/p> <\/div> <\/div>\n\n\n<div class=